post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
==> Eye-CareU was installed.

DDC/CI monitor control needs your user to be able to talk to /dev/i2c-*.
The udev rule shipped with this package puts those devices in the 'i2c'
group, so run (once):

    sudo groupadd -f i2c
    sudo usermod -aG i2c,video "$USER"
    sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger

then log out and back in (the app also re-execs itself through 'sg', so
DDC/CI normally works on the next launch without logging out).

Internal laptop panels use /sys/class/backlight and need 'video' group
membership plus the same udev trigger.

Run 'eyecareu --doctor' to check session, groups, colour backend and
every detected monitor.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
